    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability. The ASan output confirms:\n- `heap-buffer-overflow` at `decode_R13_R2000` line 1109 (the `memcmp` for the class sentinel)\n- READ of size 16 at address that is 0 bytes to the right of a 166-byte region (our exact file size)\n\nThe submission was successful with `triggered: true`.\n\nThe PoC is a 166-byte DWG R2000 file where the classes section is positioned near the end of the file with a size of 4 bytes. When `decode_R13_R2000` tries to check the class section sentinel with a 16-byte `memcmp`, it reads 10 bytes past the end of the allocated buffer because no bounds check verifies that `classes_address + 16 <= dat->size` before the comparison.",
